  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a SwiftHFR user on iOS 27, including iPhone Duo, I want the app's lists, banners, toasts and buttons outside the reader to follow Liquid Glass and use the system bars, so the app does not look older than the legacy HFR+ it replaces and its bars move to the side on the Duo cover screen.\n\nPart of #545 (M4, operator decision 2026-11-07: the HIG wins over legacy; every divergence is recorded in GAP). The full blast-radius table and HIG sources are on #545.\n\n### Scope (everything outside `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/`, except the image viewer)\n\n- **Image viewer** (`Reader/Viewer/ImageViewerView.swift`):\n  - remove the two `toolbarBackground` calls at `:24-25` and keep `.toolbarColorScheme(.dark)`;\n  - the toast at `:77` becomes `.glassEffect(in: .capsule)`;\n  - the button at `:46` becomes `.glassProminent` if it floats;\n  - `ellipsis.circle` at `:67` becomes `ellipsis`.\n- **List pagers** become a system `ToolbarItemGroup(placement: .bottomBar)` instead of `safeAreaInset` + `.background(.bar)`:\n  - `Navigation/TopicListView.swift:60-62,291`;\n  - `Messages/MessageListView.swift:62-64,170`;\n  - `Search/ForumSearchView.swift:24,128`;\n  - `FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsView.swift:115-117,196`.\n  Legacy reference: list pagers `MainWindow.swift:977-981`, filtered \"Résultats suivants\" `MessagesView.swift:4728-4740` @ `2440d79`.\n- **Top strips** with a `.bar` fill become `safeAreaBar(edge: .top)` without the fill:\n  - `TopicListView.swift:53`;\n  - `Offline/ReaderOfflineSave.swift:62`;\n  - `FilteredPostsView.swift:72`;\n  - `MessageListView.swift:191`;\n  - `Smileys/SmileyPickerView.swift:167`.\n- **Notice cards** (`regularMaterial`) **stay as materials**: HIG Materials says \"Don't use Liquid Glass in the content layer\". Only cards that float over scrolling content get glass, each one justified in the spec.\n- **Buttons:** `.glass` / `.glassProminent` only on floating controls; content-layer buttons stay.\n- **Circled toolbar symbols:** `Root/RootTabsView.swift:78`.\n- If it simplifies the code, one small `View` extension can mirror the legacy `LiquidGlass.swift` helpers.\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- the reader (LOT-186);\n- the composer bar (LOT-174, M5);\n- the Duo 27.1 APIs (LOT-147, M5);\n- the app icon (LOT-123).\n\n### Depends on\nNone merged-blocking. It runs in parallel with LOT-186 and with the docs PR for #545.\n\n### Model\nSonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5 review.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Every site above is converted or kept, with the reason in `docs/lots/LOT-185-liquid-glass-surfaces.md`, citing the HIG (URL) and the legacy file:line @ 2440d79.\n- [ ] No opaque fill remains under a bar outside the reader (grep `.background(.bar)` = 0 outside `Reader/`).\n- [ ] Model logic is unchanged; existing app tests are green, and any new view logic has a Swift Testing test.\n- [ ] SwiftLint strict is green, and so is the CI `App build + tests` job.\n- [ ] The PR has a \"Mac check needed\" section: light, dark, Dynamic Type XL, Reduce Transparency, Increase Contrast; iPhone 18 Pro, iPad and Duo poses where available.",
